# Phase 6, plan first on: nothing starts until the person has approved the
# plan they were shown. The plan is shown, sent back, changed, approved and
# started; a task added later is shown again, and the person's own start of
# it is their yes. The approval takes hold through the sweep, once the
# answer can no longer be taken back.
agent T1.1: write-result | report done "the cart is in" | hang
agent T2.1: hang
agent T3.1: hang
file brief.md: Target: the shop | Change: your part | Constraints: none | Ownership: your own files | Acceptance: the check passes
orch: init
human: set plan.first on
orch: run new "the shop"                            -> expect r1
task T1 "The cart" --name cart --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
task T2 "The search" --name search --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md

# The plan is the tool's own item, for the person alone.
orch: start T1 T2                                   -> expect exit 5 "Plan first is on" "whaleshark wait"
orch: status --items                                -> expect n1 "2 tasks"
orch: answer n1 approve                             -> expect exit 5 "the person's own click"
human: answer n1 "send back: the cart alone first"
clock +5s
orch: status --sweep --quiet
orch: wait --timeout 0                              -> expect answered "the cart alone first"

# The plan as changed: one task. Approved, it starts once the yes has settled.
orch: start T1                                      -> expect exit 5 "Plan first is on"
orch: status --items                                -> expect n2 "1 task"
human: answer n2 approve
orch: start T1                                      -> expect exit 5 "Plan first is on"
clock +5s
orch: status --sweep --quiet
orch: start T1                                      -> expect "(T1.1)"

# What is added later is shown the same way.
orch: start T2                                      -> expect exit 5 "Plan first is on"
orch: status --items                                -> expect n3 "1 more task"
human: answer n3 approve
clock +5s
orch: status --sweep --quiet
orch: start T2                                      -> expect "(T2.1)"
task T3 "The help" --name help --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
orch: start T3                                      -> expect exit 5 "Plan first is on"
human: start T3                                     -> expect "(T3.1)"
assert: attempts T1.1 reported, T2.1 working, T3.1 working; n1 state used; n2 state used; n3 state used
assert: no event lost; no event twice
